%%%
# Two-input dose-response surface: the two weight arities of §06

An unnormalized response surface over the unit square, proportional to
`dose * time^2`. The base is `iid(Uniform(interval(0, 1)), 2)` — the
unit square as a probability measure with density 1, so the weighted
density is the weight itself and the oracle is exact.

The point of the fixture is §06 `weighted`'s arity rule, scored in both
spellings over one measure:

* `w2 = (x, y) -> ...` — the k-parameter form: a weight of exactly k
  scalar parameters receives one component per parameter;
* `w1 = v -> v[1] * v[2]^2` — the one-parameter form, which receives
  the variate whole.

The scored binding is `lp = lp1 + lp2`; the two spellings denote one
measure, so a change in either alone moves the sum.

Note: the same surface over `Lebesgue(support = cartprod(...))` — the
spec's own unbinned-fit base — does NOT currently score on this path:
flatppl-js has no derivation for `builtin_logdensityof(Lebesgue, ...)`
in determinized FlatPDL (verified live 2026-09-01, 1-D included), and
the record-variate one-parameter weight is refused by the determiniser
("user call declares 1 parameter, got 2"). Both are recorded in
flatppl-dev; this fixture pins the arity rule on the base that works.
%%%
flatppl_compat = "0.1"

square = iid(Uniform(interval(0.0, 1.0)), 2)

w2 = (x, y) -> x * y^2
m2 = weighted(w2, square)
lp2 = logdensityof(m2, [0.5, 0.8])

w1 = v -> v[1] * v[2]^2
m1 = weighted(w1, square)
lp1 = logdensityof(m1, [0.5, 0.8])

lp = lp1 + lp2
